Message-ID: <DEPaQ7kJ24A.GhaFZl5GCAAJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <DEPaQ7kJ24A.4jmHhEYzCAAJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
References: <DEPaQ7kJ24A.4jmHhEYzCAAJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/DEPaQ7kJ24A/m/GhaFZl5GCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

log(area) is used because abundance is modeled on the log scale. i.e., log(lambda) = stuff.  Under the Poisson model we expect that lambda scales with area:  lambda(A) = A*lambda0.  Therefore log(A) should appear as an additive effect.

Whether you use density or abundance is purely a matter of preference.

regards
andy

