I don't see where you specified the starting values.
I suggest using some of the simpler models that produced good fits to set the starting values for the more complex models.  This sometimes will help avoid the "Hessian is singular" problem.

Alternatively, one or more parameters may simply be unidentifiable (this can happen in very small data sets or when the covariates are highly correlated).

regards
andy

